I think I messed up with this when I tried to post it.
Well here comes...

While reading the Dragonlance Legends I came upon an idea.
There are the three robes of mages: White, Red and Black.
 
So why shouldn't there be a possibility to choose ones alignment at the
beginning of the game.
 
There are currently great advantages to lawfuls (making of holy water in
their own altar) and chaotics (ability to pray in hell, they can sacrifice
humans), so there is a need to create a advantage to neutrals too.
 
There should ofcourse be some limitations to a characters alignment. For
example a knight should always be lawful and a rogue always chaotic.
Here are my suggestions of the limitations:
 
A -   N    as historians only observing
B -   N C
C - L N C
E - L   C  they see everything black or white
H - L N
K - L
P - L N C
R -     C
S - L N
T - L N C
W - L N C      

the others are quite obvious.
This could make a lawful priest _very_ powerful character indeed..

So please let me know what you think.

